## Build & Test

```bash
# Install dependencies
npm install

# Run Metro bundler
npm start

# Android (requires Android SDK in Windows)
npm run android

# iOS (requires macOS)
npm run ios

# Tests
npm test

# Lint
npm run lint

# Final gate check
npm run gate
```

## Clean Architecture Structure

```
src/
├── api/              # Data Layer: API clients (Supabase, S3)
├── assets/           # Static files: Images, fonts, icons
├── components/       # Presentation Layer: Global UI primitives
├── core/             # Shared Layer: Constants, themes, configuration
├── features/         # Domain Layer: Feature-based modules
│   └── files/        # Example feature directory
│       ├── components/  # Feature-specific UI
│       ├── hooks/       # Feature-specific logic (Data fetching, State)
│       ├── screens/     # High-level screen components
│       ├── services/    # Business logic / Use cases
│       └── types.ts     # Feature-specific TypeScript interfaces
├── navigation/       # Routing: Stack and Tab navigators
├── store/            # Global State: Context providers or Zustand/Redux
└── utils/            # Helper functions: Formatters, validators
```

## Step 2.5 Internal Audit (Mobile-Specific)

Before Kilo Review, verify:
- [ ] **Strict Typing:** All navigation parameters and API responses explicitly typed
- [ ] **Hook Isolation:** Complex screen logic moved into custom hooks (e.g., `useFileUpload`)
- [ ] **Native Module Bloat:** No unnecessary native dependencies
- [ ] **Permission Over-privilege:** Request only necessary Android/iOS permissions
- [ ] **Metro Bundler:** Test bundle generation with `npx react-native bundle`

## Security

- No hardcoded API keys or tokens
- Use environment variables for all config
- Validate all user inputs before API calls
- Run as non-root user in production containers

## Mobile One-Test Rule Example

```markdown
## One-Test Rule

**Why:** The biggest risk in automated mobile deployment is a broken Metro Bundler 
configuration or native module mismatch.

**Contract:**
- **Given:** A fresh environment with the current package.json
- **When:** The agent executes `npx react-native bundle --platform android --dev false`
- **Then:** It must produce a valid index.bundle without syntax or dependency errors
- **Mocked:** Native hardware APIs (Camera, GPS, etc.)
- **Real:** Metro bundler, TypeScript compiler, React Native packager
```

## Conventions

- **Feature-based modules:** Keep related code together in `src/features/*`
- **Type-safe navigation:** All routes defined in `src/navigation/types.ts`
- **Custom hooks:** Extract complex logic from screens
- **No "Massive Component" syndrome:** Max 200 lines per screen component
